{#
  The Corefile key of kube-system/coredns, and nothing else. k3s's node controller writes
  `NodeHosts` into this ConfigMap and keeps writing it, so Flux never declares the key. Under
  server-side apply a key the render omits stays with its writer. Declaring `NodeHosts` here
  would fight the controller, and applying a ConfigMap with an empty one would blank the node
  names no pod could then resolve until the next node event.
  ansible/roles/k8s/coredns/tests/test_coredns_render.py holds the one-key rule.

  Keep comments at column 0 and above the document: an indented comment between two keys would
  land inside the block scalar.
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: coredns
  namespace: kube-system
data:
  Corefile: |
{{ lookup('template', playbook_dir + '/roles/k8s/coredns/templates/config/coredns-corefile.j2') | indent(4, true) }}
